# Pairs with NoKeyLost. The online snapshot copies nothing, so after the flip
# the resized copy holds none of the rows written before the resize began.
MODULE: NoKeyLostSnapshotSkipsRows
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the snapshot copies no committed rows, so the resized copy loses every pre-resize key at the flip
PERTURBS: SnapCopy

--- FIND
    /\ row' = [x \in Copies |-> [s \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |->
                 IF x = R /\ s \in rzShards /\ MapOf(rmapR, k) = s
                 THEN Max(row[R][s][k], row[T][s][k]) ELSE row[x][s][k]]]]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no committed entries are copied.
    /\ UNCHANGED row
--- END